From 5d1e7f0ef129581d6b171327817e943316072cf8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Port Bot <port@local>
Date: Wed, 13 May 2026 15:28:49 +0200
Subject: feat: namespace filtering by user/system origin

- Introduce a new `--non-system-namespaces-prefix` bridge flag (also
  available as `BRIDGE_NON_SYSTEM_NAMESPACES_PREFIX`) on the backend
  that is propagated to the frontend through
  `window.SERVER_FLAGS.nonSystemNamespacesPrefix`, so deployments with
  bespoke tenant prefixes can opt-out of the system-namespace
  classification without rebuilding the console image.
- Update `isSystemNamespace()` to honour the new allow-prefix list:
  anything that does not match either a known system prefix or one of
  the configured non-system prefixes is treated as system, keeping the
  default namespace dropdown free of operator/tenant churn.
- Replace the hardcoded prefix array in `console-shared/constants` with
  a getter that reads `SERVER_FLAGS.nonSystemNamespacesPrefix`, so the
  list is fully driven from the backend.

Consolidates the original 0024/0043/0046 patches.
